# XCU bg
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# bg is intrinsic (XCU 1.7). What bg does in a shell that is not
# interactive is left optional by the page; so one test is run with job
# control disabled in the shell running the test, and the other in an
# interactive shell started with sh -i whose input is a script. That test
# reports UNRESOLVED when the interactive shell does not have job control
# enabled.

assertion  XCU.bg.001
anchor     utilities/bg.html#CONSEQUENCES OF ERRORS
anchor     utilities/bg.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       With job control disabled, bg exits greater than zero, writes
           nothing to standard output and puts no job into the
           background.
test       t/001-disabled.sh

assertion  XCU.bg.002
anchor     utilities/bg.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/bg.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.11
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       In an interactive shell with job control, bg job_id resumes a
           suspended job as a background job, writes a line [number]
           command, exits zero, and the job runs again (jobs reports it
           Running).
test       t/002-resume.sh

assertion  XCU.bg.003
anchor     utilities/bg.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       In an interactive shell with job control, bg for a job that is
           already running in the background has no effect and exits
           zero.
test       t/003-already-running.sh
